Section 7.1. The Borrower shall maintain, as of each fiscal year-end, measured using year-end balances:

(a) a ratio of total current assets to total current liabilities of not less than 1.80 to 1.00;

(b) a ratio of total liabilities to total stockholders' equity of not more than 1.10 to 1.00;

(c) a ratio of operating income to interest expense (times interest earned) of not less than 6.50 to 1.00; and

(d) cash dividends paid during the fiscal year not exceeding 75% of net income for that year.
